cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "Biology as Code: an open, provenance-tracked toolkit for meal digestion and metabolic-pathway modeling, incl. the FDP-1 Food Data Provenance Declaration"
abstract: >-
  biology-as-code is an open-source toolkit that models what happens to a meal —
  digestion, absorption, and the metabolic pathways it drives — as inspectable code:
  a meal-simulation pipeline, a declarative model of the GI tract as versioned state
  machines, teaching metabolic-pathway graphs, LAW-SPEC law cards as queryable data, and
  an evidence/provenance layer. This release also publishes FDP-1, the Food Data
  Provenance Declaration — a minimal specification for declaring the provenance of a
  nutrient value and the validation status of any score computed from such values —
  together with a reference validator, the MASTER_CROSSWALK ID spine, and a worked
  example. Built to be fail-closed with no fabricated data. Teaching / research software;
  not medical advice.
